# Platform is running the review agent's judge calls on Groq (Llama 3.3 70B) — not
# to be confused with xAI's Grok model, similar name only. Standalone default in
# this repo's own config.py is still "anthropic"; the root docker-compose.yml
# overrides that via REVIEW_AGENT_LLM_PROVIDER when running the full stack.
LLM_PROVIDER=groq
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# LLM_PROVIDER=xai
# XAI_API_KEY=xai-...
# XAI_MODEL=grok-4

# Required when running via `docker compose up` (review-agent runs itself as a container
# and talks to the *host* Docker daemon to launch dynamic-test sibling containers). Must be
# an absolute path that exists on the host — docker-compose.yml bind-mounts it into
# review-agent's own container at the identical path, so a tempdir review-agent creates
# under it is also a valid bind-mount source for the sibling containers it launches.
# Not needed when running bare-metal via review_cli.py.
DYNAMIC_TEST_OUTPUTS_DIR=/absolute/path/to/review-agent/.dynamic-test-outputs
